@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Cookie Policy";
    var supportAddress = Configuration["Email:SupportAddress"] ?? "support@example.test";
}

<section class="policy-hero">
    <div class="shell policy-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Cookie Policy</p>
        <h1>A clear record of browser storage used by the service.</h1>
        <p>Effective 28 August 2026 · Version @LegalDocumentVersions.Cookies</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="policy-page">
    <div class="shell policy-layout">
        <aside class="policy-summary">
            <strong>Current choice</strong>
            <p>Only essential security cookies are used. Analytics, advertising, and cross-site tracking cookies are not used.</p>
            <button class="button button-secondary button-small" type="button" data-cookie-reset>Show cookie notice again</button>
        </aside>
        <article class="policy-document">
            <section><h2>1. What cookies are</h2><p>Cookies are small values a website stores in a browser. Similar local-storage technologies can remember preferences on a device. This policy explains both.</p></section>
            <section>
                <h2>2. Essential cookies</h2>
                <div class="policy-table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Typical duration</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>JobTracker.Auth</code></td><td>Keeps an authenticated user signed in and protects the private workspace.</td><td>Up to 8 hours, with sliding renewal when active.</td></tr><tr><td><code>JobTracker.Antiforgery</code></td><td>Helps prevent another site from submitting forms as you.</td><td>Session or request lifecycle.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
                <p>These cookies are strictly necessary for account sign-in and security. They cannot be disabled through an in-app preference without making the authenticated service unusable. You can block them in the browser, but sign-in and protected forms will not work correctly.</p>
            </section>
            <section><h2>3. Local browser preferences</h2><p>The service uses local storage for the selected light or dark theme, application-list display preference, and the record that the essential-cookie notice was acknowledged. These values remain on the device until cleared through browser settings or the available in-app control.</p></section>
            <section><h2>4. No optional tracking cookies</h2><p>The current service does not use analytics, advertising, profiling, social-media, or cross-site tracking cookies. Because no optional cookie category is active, there is no misleading “accept all” option. If optional cookies are introduced, they will remain disabled until an appropriate choice is obtained.</p></section>
            <section><h2>5. Managing storage</h2><p>You can clear cookies and local storage in your browser. Clearing the authentication cookie signs you out. Clearing local preferences resets the theme, display preferences, and cookie-notice acknowledgement on that device.</p></section>
            <section><h2>6. Contact</h2><p>Questions about cookies or browser storage can be sent to <a href="mailto:@supportAddress">@supportAddress</a>.</p></section>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>
